#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background"
msgstr "Antecedentes"

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "About &digikam;"
msgstr "Sobre &digikam;"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:7
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&digikam; is an advanced digital photo management application for the &kde; desktop. It provides a simple interface which makes importing and organizing digital photographs a &quot;snap&quot;. &digikam; enables you to manage large numbers of digital photographs in Albums and to organize these photographs for easy retrieval using tags (keywords), captions, collections, dates, geolocation and searches. It has many features for viewing, organizing, processing and sharing your images. Thus, &digikam; is a formidable <link linkend=\"dam\">Digital Asset Management</link> (DAM) software including powerful image editing functions."
msgid "&digikam; is an advanced digital photo management application for Linux, MacOS and Windows desktop. It provides a simple interface which makes importing and organizing digital photographs a &quot;snap&quot;. &digikam; enables you to manage large numbers of digital photographs in Albums and to organize these photographs for easy retrieval using tags (keywords), captions, collections, dates, geolocation and searches. It has many features for viewing, organizing, processing and sharing your images. Thus, &digikam; is a formidable <link linkend=\"using-dam\">Digital Asset Management</link> (DAM) software including powerful image editing functions."
msgstr "O &digikam; é un aplicativo avanzado de xestión de fotos dixitais para o escritorio &kde;. Fornece unha interface simple que fai que importar e organizar fotografías dixitais sexa cousa de nada. O &digikam; permite xestionar grandes cantidades de fotografías dixitais en álbums e organizalas para recuperalas facilmente usando etiquetas (palabras chave), títulos, coleccións, datas, localización xeográfica e buscas. Dispón de moitas funcionalidades para ver, organizar, procesar e compartir as imaxes. Así, o &digikam; é software formidábel para a <link linkend=\"dam\">Xestión de recursos dixitais</link> (DAM) e inclúe funcións potentes de edición dixital."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:11
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "An easy-to-use Camera interface is provided, that will connect to your digital camera and download photographs directly into &digikam; Albums. More than <ulink url=\"http://www.gphoto.org/proj/libgphoto2/support.php\">1000 digital cameras</ulink> are supported by the gphoto2 library. Of course, any media or card reader supported by your operating system will interface with &digikam;."
msgid "An easy-to-use Camera interface is provided that will connect to your digital camera and download photographs directly into &digikam; Albums. More than <ulink url=\"http://www.gphoto.org/proj/libgphoto2/support.php\">1000 digital cameras</ulink> are supported by the gphoto2 library. Of course, any media or card reader supported by your operating system will interface with &digikam;."
msgstr "Dispón dunha interface para cámaras doada de usar que se conecta coas cámaras dixitais e descarga as fotografías directamente para os álbums de &digikam;. Recoñece máis de <ulink url=\"http://www.gphoto.org/proj/libgphoto2/support.php\">1000 cámaras dixitais</ulink> grazas á biblioteca gphoto2. Pode acceder, por suposto, a calquera dispositivo ou lector de tarxetas que recoñeza o sistema operativo."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:15
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&digikam; incorporates a fast Image Editor with many image editing tools. You can use the Image Editor to view your photographs, comment and rate them, correct, enhance and alter them. The editing power can be easily extended by a set of plugins, the <ulink url=\"http://www.kipi-plugins.org\">Kde Image Plugins Interface</ulink> (<ulink url=\"help:/kipi-plugins/index.html\">manual</ulink>)"
msgid "&digikam; incorporates a fast Image Editor with many image editing tools. You can use the Image Editor to view your photographs, comment and rate them, correct, enhance and alter them. The images post processing can be easily done by a set of tools though the Batch Queue Manager, or by many import and export tools dedicated to work with remote web services."
msgstr "O &digikam; incorpora un editor de imaxes rápido con moitas ferramentas para a edición de imaxes. Pódese usar para ver as fotografías, comentalas e puntualas, corrixilas, melloralas e alteralas. A súa potencia de edición pode ser estendida facilmente cun conxunto de engadidos, a <ulink url=\"http://www.kipi-plugins.org\">Inferface de engadidos de imaxe de KDE</ulink> (<ulink url=\"help:/kipi-plugins/index.html\">manual</ulink>)"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:21
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "While &digikam; remains easy to use, it provides professional level features by the dozens. It is fully 16 bit enabled including all available plugins, supports RAW format conversion through libraw, DNG export and ICC color management <link linkend=\"rawprocessing.anchor\">work flow</link>."
msgid "While &digikam; remains easy to use, it provides professional level features by the dozens. It is fully 16 bit enabled including all available tools, supports RAW format conversion through libraw, DNG export and ICC color management <link linkend=\"rawprocessing.anchor\">work flow</link>."
msgstr "Mesmo se &digikam; resulta doado de usar, fornece funcionalidades de nivel profesional a moreas. É totalmente compatíbel con 16 bits, incluídos todos os complementos dispoñíbeis, admite a conversión do formato RAW mediante libraw, a exportación a DNG e a xestión de cor ICC."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reporting Bugs"
msgstr "Informes de fallos"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:29
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Like the rest of &kde;, &digikam; is an Open Source project. This means that it relies on its users to play their part by, at least, reporting problems and suggesting possible improvements."
msgid "&digikam; is an Open Source project. This means that it relies on its users to play their part by, at least, reporting problems and suggesting possible improvements."
msgstr "Como o resto de &kde;, o &digikam; é un proxecto de Código Aberto. Isto significa que confía en que os usuarios cumpran co seu papel, informando como mínimo dos problemas e suxerindo posíbeis melloras."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid "&digikam; makes it as easy as possible for you to report bugs or suggest improvements. Wherever you are in the application the Help menu will include a Report Bugs option. This will display a message box with a highlighted link. Click on the link and your web browser will open the page for the reporting system. All the information required will already be filled in, just follow the instructions for completing your report."
msgstr "&digikam; facilita o máis que pode o informe de fallos e a suxestión de melloras. Sempre que se estea no aplicativo, o menú Axuda inclúe unha opción Informar de fallos. isto fai aparecer unha caixa de mensaxe cunha ligazón realzada. Prema a ligazón e o navegador web abre a páxina do sistema de informe de fallos. Toda a información requirida xa está introducida. Simplemente siga as instrucións para completar o informe."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "Support"
msgstr "Asistencia técnica"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:42
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&digikam; is a community supported project, which means that users and developers support one another. If you become a regular user of &digikam; you are encouraged to join the &digikam; Users Mailing List. You can start off by asking questions of other &digikam; users and hopefully soon you will be answering the support questions of others."
msgid "&digikam; is a community supported project, which means that users and developers support one another. If you become a regular user of &digikam; you are encouraged to join the &digikam; Users Mailing List. You can start off by asking questions to other &digikam; users and hopefully soon you will be answering the support questions of others."
msgstr "&digikam; é un proxecto apoiado pola comunidade, o que significa que os usuarios e os desenvolvedores se axudan mutuamente. Se vostede decide ser un usuario habitual do &digikam;, por favor, únase á Lista de correo dos usuarios do &digikam;. Pode comezar facéndolles preguntas a outros usuarios e pronto se pode ver respondendo as dúbidas que outros teñan."

#. Tag: ulink
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "&digikam; Users Mailing List joining instructions."
msgstr "Instrucións para unirse á lista de correo dos usuarios de &digikam;."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:51
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "You can also visit the <ulink url=\"http://www.digikam.org\">&digikam; Home Page.</ulink> for news of new releases and other &digikam; related information."
msgid "You can also visit the <ulink url=\"http://www.digikam.org\">&digikam; Home Page</ulink> for news of new releases and other &digikam; related information."
msgstr "Tamén pode visitar a <ulink url=\"http://www.digikam.org\">páxina web de &digikam;</ulink> para ver noticias sobre novas versións e outra información relacionada con &digikam;."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Involved"
msgstr "Participación"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are many ways that you can get involved with the continued development of &digikam;. You do not need to be a software developer. You can help with documentation, translation and user interface design or just contribute really good ideas to the wish-list. You can also get involved by testing early development code as it is being developed and providing feedback to the developers. Of course, if you are a software developer then you can help to make &digikam; the best digital photograph application there is."
msgstr "Hai moitas maneiras de participar no desenvolvemento continuado de &digikam;. Non hai por que ser un desenvolvedor. Pódese axudar coa documentación, a tradución e o deseño da interface de usuario ou simplemente aportar boas ideas á lista de desexos. Tamén se pode participar probando as primeiras versións do código en desenvolvemento segundo se vai creando e fornecéndolles opinións aos desenvolvedores. Por suposto, se sabe programar pode axudar a que &digikam; sexa o mellor aplicativo de fotografía dixital que existe."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-background.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "The best way to start getting involved with &digikam; is to join the Developers Mailing List. <ulink url=\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/digikam-devel\">&digikam; Developer Mailing List joining instructions.</ulink>"
msgstr "A mellor maneira de comezar a colaborar con &digikam; é unirse á lista de correo dos desenvolvedores. <ulink url=\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/digikam-devel\">Instrucións para unirse á lista de correo dos desenvolvedores de &digikam;.</ulink>"
